From: Kirill =?UTF-8?q?M=C3=BCller?= <kirill@cynkra.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Define D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED whenever D_ASSERT is live

assert.hpp has two branches. A release build takes the one that includes
<assert.h> and defines D_ASSERT as assert; a debug build takes the one
that routes D_ASSERT through DuckDBAssertInternal() and defines
D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED, so that code needed only by an assertion can be
compiled out of a release build.

The two disagree when NDEBUG is undefined and DEBUG is not defined.
assert() then checks its condition, so every D_ASSERT is live, while
D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED stays undefined and the code it guards is compiled
out -- including a helper that a D_ASSERT calls. Where such a helper
exists this is a compile error rather than a silent difference:
src/function/variant/variant_shredding.cpp guards IsVariantStringType()
and calls it from the D_ASSERT in WriteShreddedString().

That combination is not exotic. R's pkgbuild compiles a package with
-UNDEBUG -Wall -pedantic -g -O0 for devtools::load_all(), so the R
package fails to build on that file while R CMD INSTALL of the same tree
succeeds.

Define D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED in the <assert.h> branch too whenever NDEBUG
is not defined. The macro then means on both branches what its name
says, and assert-only code is compiled exactly when the assertions that
need it are checked.

Staged in krlmlr/duckdb on branch assert-is-enabled-without-ndebug, to
go to duckdb/duckdb from there, and carried here until a release carries
it.
---
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/assert.hpp b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/assert.hpp
index 4bf4b90..0e8fd13 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/assert.hpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/include/duckdb/common/assert.hpp
@@ -25,6 +25,11 @@
 //! Only the 'else' condition is supposed to check the assertions
 #include <assert.h>
 #define D_ASSERT assert
+//! assert() checks its condition whenever NDEBUG is not defined, so the
+//! assert-only code that D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED guards has to be compiled here too
+#ifndef NDEBUG
+#define D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED
+#endif
 namespace duckdb {
 DUCKDB_API void DuckDBAssertInternal(bool condition, const char *condition_name, const char *file, int linenr);
 }
